							<h3>In summary, the advantages of polypropylene filter bags are mainly reflected in:</h3><ul><li><strong>Chemical Resistance</strong>: suitable for filtering a variety of chemical media.</li><li><strong>Thermal Stability</strong>: has high heat resistance and can usually be used in the temperature range of 80~100℃.</li><li><strong>High Strength</strong>: polypropylene fiber has high mechanical strength and can withstand high operating pressure and flow rate.</li></ul><hr /><h3>Specifications</h3><table border="0" width="1079" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><tbody><tr><td class="et3" width="384" height="29">Brand Name</td><td class="et3" width="695">Filmedia</td></tr><tr><td class="et3" height="29">Material</td><td class="et3">Non-woven Polypropylene Needle Felt</td></tr><tr><td class="et3" height="29">Maximum operating temperature</td><td class="et3">80-100℃</td></tr><tr><td class="et3" height="29">Mesh Count (per inch)</td><td class="et3">26000-60</td></tr><tr><td class="et3" height="29">Filtartion Area (square meters)</td><td class="et3">0.75</td></tr><tr><td class="et3" height="29">Filtration Accurancy (μm)</td><td class="et3">0.5-200</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 class="wp-block-heading has-text-align-left">Philite® Exclusive Features</h3><ul><li>Gradual mesh count structure.</li><li>Suitable for standard filter housings.</li><li>Unique manufacturing process enables 62% more filtration area in per unit.</li><li>4 times life expectancy than conventional filter bag.</li><li>Better contamination absorption.</li><li>Highly increased filtration traffic in per unit.</li><li>Easy disposal and replacement, minimum time consumption and cost effective.</li><li>Latest technology and production concept in Filmedia system and filtration basket design.</li><li>100% three-dimension support for filter medium, eliminate the potential breaking threat. Compare to traditional filter bags, 3D-support design extremely decreases contamination retention.</li></ul>						</div>
